  "id": "DrugBank_DB01225 - MONDO_809",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Enoxaparin and Purpura Fulminans, mediated through Pulmonary Embolism (disease). Enoxaparin, a low-molecular-weight heparin, is indicated for Pulmonary Embolism, and this indication is shared with Heparin, Bovine and Adomiparin, all of which are linked to Purpura Fulminans. This indicates that Enoxaparin may exert a biological effect that contributes to the development of Purpura Fulminans, possibly through mechanisms involving anticoagulant activity or other pharmacological properties. The shared indication pathways suggest a possible mechanism of action that could be relevant to the pathophysiology of Purpura Fulminans, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence is supported by a consistent pathway linking Enoxaparin to Pulmonary Embolism, which in turn is associated with Purpura Fulminans, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct causal relationship.",
